 them so they're  easier to accurately type on and they're  now click here as well but with less key  travel overall the keyboard is well  above average and most people will be  happy with it  the trackpad is also an improvement over  last year's model being slightly larger  and easier to click making this one of  the better track pads available in  Windows  speakers have been one of our major  complaints with Dell laptops but just  like with other things they've been  listening last year's XPS 13 had only  one watt speakers the new two-in-one  doubled that to 2 watts each  and this XPS gets two and a half watts  per speaker it's still not as loud as  the surface laptop three but at this  point they are loud enough and the sound  quality is above average being better  than the surface when I saw that this  thing got slimmer I immediately figured  that the SSD would be soldered just like  the two and one but I was thrilled to  see that it's user replaceable which is  impressive in a laptop so small if you  choose to pay $50 extra you get 512 gigs  like we did and I definitely would  suggest it since this isn't a low budget  SSD ours got about twenty six hundred  megabytes per second read and twenty two  hundred megabytes per second right it's  also packin some killer Wireless specs  like Bluetooth five and top the line  Wi-Fi six reception is a bit worse than  the surface laptop three in the toughest  part of my basement but still much  better than the new MacBook Air which  lacks Wi-Fi six asked for ports we got a  micro SD card slot and two full-speed  Thunderbolt 3 ports like the two and one  but we no longer have that extra  standard USB C port like last year now  let's get into performance benchmarks  where we'll compare our i7 to last  year's i7 in Geekbench five CPU tests  we're seeing about 30% higher scores  compared to last year which is  especially impressive since we know it's  more efficient than before when pushing  the new XPS to its limits and Cinebench  r20 is scored over 40% higher than the  previous best two gigahertz i7 as for  the graphics it's even more impressive  we went from fifty seven hundred to ten  thousand four hundred and twenty which  is over eighty percent faster graphics  performance since much more apps are now  using graphics acceleration this can  really help out now this definitely  isn't a gaming laptop but in firestrike  the g7 graphics destroyed last year's u  HD graphics so you should be able to get  away with some light gaming  finally the  life expect 9 to 10 hours of real-world  mixed-use if you get the 1080p model but  if you do have the 4k screen like we do  it's more like 5 to 6 hours which can be  a bummer the 4k screen is gorgeous  though which makes it a tough choice  personally I wish Dell went the way of  Microsoft and Apple and stopped making  us choose and just gave us a resolution  somewhere in between which can offer  both good battery life and a nice  viewing experience my second complaint  is the prices at the time of this video  the standard XPS 13 costs more than the  XPS 2 and one and more than some of the  competition but I know that Dell usually  runs discounts after a bit so once the  price is lower I would have no  hesitation recommending this laptop the  performance is excellent the build  quality is top-notch the keyboard and  trackpad are good speakers are now above  average  we now have Windows hello and an easily  swappable SSD and battery for future  proofing honestly even if it costs a bit  more if you need a top notch Windows  Ultrabook this one is almost perfect if  you enjoy this review make sure that's  how that like button and click the  circle above so you can see us compare  it to a 13-inch MacBook Pro thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  video  [Music]
 

